massive platform.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:15.440
To give you an
idea, we monitor--

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.980
in this time series database
that we have internally,

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:21.210
we monitor more than
3 billion resources,

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.940
roughly about 480
terabytes of RAM,

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.120
because it's a highly
distributed in-memory time

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.700
series database.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.540
On our logging backend,
we have in a day,

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.334
roughly 35 petabytes of data.

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:34.750
So it's a massive infrastructure
that we have, and now are

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:37.650
putting outside for all
of you to use and take

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:38.929
advantage of that.

00:08:38.929 --> 00:08:42.179
Stackdriver is built on
top of that infrastructure.

00:08:42.179 --> 00:08:44.250
And so what we do is
we use that and then

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.990
we create a set of tools
that we have exposed

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:47.990
to all of our customers.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.490
So we can do visualizations,
use them in dashboards,

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:53.040
create multi-conditioning
alerts,

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.290
