00:24:05.700 --> 00:24:08.010
And just let me try to
orient ourselves here

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:09.600
a little bit on this console.

00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:12.490
On the upper side,
you see that widget--

00:24:12.490 --> 00:24:13.740
it's the event timeline.

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:15.080
It's our event widget.

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:18.360
What we're trying to do here
is surface Kubernetes events

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:20.320
that may be relevant to you.

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:22.540
And this is actually a heat map.

00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:26.034
So you see the more
transparent colors?

00:24:26.034 --> 00:24:28.200
The more solid colors
actually have higher frequency

00:24:28.200 --> 00:24:29.070
of events.

00:24:29.070 --> 00:24:33.340
The less solid ones are
less events and so on.

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.680
Now you modify time
sets and other things.

00:24:35.680 --> 00:24:38.610
But the important thing here is
that we want to surface events

00:24:38.610 --> 00:24:41.310
that you can then correlate with
the state of your Kubernetes

00:24:41.310 --> 00:24:42.450
environment.

00:24:42.450 --> 00:24:44.910
Today, in beta,
we're just surfacing

00:24:44.910 --> 00:24:46.960
events related to incidents.

00:24:46.960 --> 00:24:49.140
Now, incidents are
essentially violations

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:51.000
of your alerting policies.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:53.876
So you created alerting
policies by defining

00:24:53.876 --> 00:24:55.500
[INAUDIBLE] conditions
that you believe

00:24:55.500 --> 00:24:59.105
are your own notion
of health, right?

00:24:59.105 --> 00:25:01.230
Something you would say
this is, when this happens,

00:25:01.230 --> 00:25:06.460
most likely a failure or a
situation we want to avoid,

00:25:06.460 --> 00:25:08.380
perhaps, is likely to occur.

00:25:08.380 --> 00:25:09.600
So we want to use those.

00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:11.640
When a failure occurs,
we create an incident.

00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:13.650
And those are the ones
you're seeing here.

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:16.590
Now, let's focus our
