00:27:41.730 --> 00:27:43.290
for you.

00:27:43.290 --> 00:27:46.650
So now it's really logs that
are only relevant for that pod,

00:27:46.650 --> 00:27:49.526
for that particular period
of time, events and metadata

00:27:49.526 --> 00:27:51.900
that are only relevant for
that particular period of time

00:27:51.900 --> 00:27:52.734
in those components.

00:27:52.734 --> 00:27:54.566
And that's what I meant
earlier about trying

00:27:54.566 --> 00:27:57.270
to increase the observability
of your Kubernetes environment,

00:27:57.270 --> 00:28:00.230
not just having you to look for
those things in separate tools

00:28:00.230 --> 00:28:01.860
all together, but
rather bringing

00:28:01.860 --> 00:28:03.660
